you probably already know this but games  are hard to make and often  don't always get released with their  original vision intact  from a gameplay pivot here to a  character swap there  most go through some pretty big changes  throughout their development  but then there are some games that  change course completely  here are seven games you might not know  were originally  something else entirely hot off the  heels of releasing prince of persia  signs of time  in 2003 the team at ubisoft montreal was  tasked with making a follow-up for the  xbox 360 and playstation 3.  according to director patrice desolay  the team's mandate was to  redefine the action adventure genre  which was no mean feat  the original vision for the game was to  take the parkour gameplay from prince  and put it into an open world the move  to next gen also enabled the team to put  cut ideas from sands of time  into the game including crowds and the  ability to jump from rooftop to rooftop  over the course of development desolate  came to realize that a prince  wasn't exactly an exciting character to  play as  quote i wanted the prince to have a  different job than just being there  waiting for mom and dad to die and take  their place  during his research he uncovered a book  about secret societies  and one that caught his eye was the  assassins and so the player would play  as an assassin  protecting an ai controlled prince the  project was originally titled prince of  persia assassins  but as desolate and the team  incorporated more of the secret society  stuff  the prince eventually ended up being cut  it wasn't until gdc 2006 that ubisoft  marketing suggested the title we've all  come to know and love  assassin's creed halo may have redefined  the console first person shooter but  originally  it was not first person at all or even a  shooter  or even a console game halo originally  started life as an isometric real-time  strategy game  more in line with bungie's previous  franchise myth the game eventually  changed to a third person perspective  when the developers realized that it was  more fun to actually control the game's  vehicles  than letting the computer do it the game  was unveiled at mac world in 1999 by  none other than steve  jobs but after some financial  difficulties bungie ended up being  bought by microsoft a year later  and halo was being shaped to be the  upcoming xbox consoles flagship game  halo's perspective changed once again  this time to first person  and the story and world was cemented the  rest as they say is history  if you want the full story check out our  episode of remember when  all about the game's origin look i could  do  a whole video about the tumultuous  development of resident evil 4.  at least four versions of that game were  conceptualized and then ultimately  scrapped  but let's focus on the version that  eventually became devil may cry  early in development resident evil 4 was  in the hands of resident evil 2 director  hideki kamia  who wanted to make resident evil a  little cooler  time to go to work guys  the protagonist tony was originally a  superhuman upgraded by biotechnology  resident evil series producer shinji  mikami felt that the coolness angle  didn't really fit with the resident evil  franchise and so the game was spun off  and became its own thing this one's  pretty well known but a very cool story  nonetheless  back in the early 80s nintendo was  struggling to break into the american  market  and had thousands of unsold arcade  machines that needed to be salvaged  a young designer by the name of shigeru  miyamoto was brought on to create a game  that could hopefully sell these cabinets  to try and be more appealing to the  american audience  nintendo attempted to get the license  for popeye but when that all fell  through  mimoto apes the love triangle between  bluto olive oil and popeye with  donkey kong a carpenter who would  eventually become mario and his  girlfriend  pauline  [Music]  splinter cell started life by being  shuffled around various ubisoft studios  in paris it was an rts game upon landing  in new york it became an action  adventure title called the drift  where the world's major cities were  floating around in the sky on  islands playing as buster these are my  awards mother  from army no not that one you could  control flying vehicles and the game's  ai meant that crowds would react  appropriately  to your actions it also had a modular  weapon that could allow players to  grapple up walls  the drift sadly was going nowhere and  ubisoft eventually tried to pitch it as  a james bond game  but it didn't get picked up eventually  the project made its way to montreal and  was to be the metal gear solid 2  killer ubisoft's idea was to get one  over on metal gear by attaching tom  clancy's name  and releasing on the platform that metal  gear wasn't available on  microsoft quickly bought onto the idea  and helped optimize and market the game  this video you're looking at right now  is what borderlands  used to be gone is the colorful  cel-shaded art style and wacky humor and  what we originally had instead was  a pretty po-faced sci-fi title the  original pitch was halo  meets diablo and the game's artists were  given inspiration words like  serious gritty and realistic  however testers within gearbox deemed  the game's art style to be too similar  to fallout 3 and there was a huge  discrepancy  between the game's realistic look and  its bombastic  over-the-top gameplay at the 11th hour  the developer changed the art style to  what we recognized today  bioshock is such an impactful and  memorable game it's hard to think that  it might have been  completely different in the original  pitch you were to take on the role of  carlos coelho  a deprogrammer assigned to infiltrate a  religious cult called serene dawn  and rescue a wealthy heiress the player  was able to create  any weapon they wanted from a set of  attributes and components  and modify them at will there was  definitely hacking aplenty in bioshock  but the original plans were much  grander you would be able to hack the  environment increasing and decreasing  oxygen levels  manipulate gravity electrify flaws and  even adjust the temperature  instead of attacking splices the enemy  types would be human cultists  cyborg killers genetically engineered  mammal aquatic hybrids  and robots it also had grand ideas for a  multiplayer component  where you'd play as the enemy monster in  someone else's story mode  irrational games released their old  design documents online if you want to  go back  and see the bioshock that might have  been those are seven games that were  originally something else entirely  come find me on twitter and talk to me  about bioshock i'm at lucy james games  we'll see you next time  you
 

